  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Orange Corners: Pre-programme in Korhogo, San Pedro and Vavoua,</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to support youth to access entrepreneurship opportunities in the cocoa, horticulture, and circular economy sectors in Vavoua, Korhogo and San Pedro, the Northern region of C&#xF4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire.This objective is pursued through two primary initiatives:&#x2022;	Empowering young people, through the design sprint training sessions to stimulate their entrepreneurial mindset, increase their knowledge of the horticulture, cocoa and circular economy sectors, including insights into various business opportunities within these industries. &#x2022;	Facilitating engagement with Dutch-Orange Corners; this initiative aims to stimulate inclusion of young agripreneurs from more rural areas to become participants in the Dutch funded Orange Corners programme. Additionally, the project gives these young agripreneurs a chance to connect with the Dutch private sector and get involved in opportunities. Moreover, it aims to improve collaboration in the entrepreneurial ecosystem between public and private stakeholders, as well as at an Ivorian-Dutch level.</narrative>
  </description>
